💭 A new list assigned over a variable that holds a list.
💭
💭 Expected: memory stays as it is.
💭 What happens: the new list is built in the variable's place without the old one being
💭 released (ASTVariableInit::generate), so the old list and what it holds are leaked.
💭 The same is so for a dictionary.
💭
💭 Emptying the list with 🐗 is fine, and so is building the new list in a variable of
💭 its own and assigning that.
